    "text": "With temperatures in Scotland region predicted to increase by 1.59o\ud436in the next 50 years, current models project the Atlantic mackerel to migrate away from northwestern Scotland and towards the general direction of Iceland. While populations of mackerel may still dot the coasts of Scotland in the future, the numbers are predicted to be substantially less than current values. Even worse, the models for Atlantic herring forecast herring to move northwest to the re- gion just east of Iceland by 2070, leaving no herring within \ufb01shing radius from the coasts of Scotland. The southern and western coasts of Scotland are expected to be most impacted by this migration, losing access $1.00"
  },
